+Q251 /261C: A NONWRAPPING CHART REFINEMENT WITH A NEW INVISIBLE FIELD
+11November2026. Frozen analytical candidate, awaiting source audit.
+This is a grouped research result, not a standalone paper, PDF or grade.
+It is NOT inferred by splitting a previously invisible cyclic cell sum.
+The cutoff below is constructed anew to kill every refined cell separately.
+
+ACTUAL MODEL AND ACTUAL CANONICAL PARTITION
+Let n=2^m,m>=5,c>0,a=c/48,H=cn^2,V=n^3. Use the original D3 orthogonal
+checkerboard forward form and counting norm, with channel1 strong at odd
+sources, channel2 strong at even sources, actual U0^2=im(d1^*)^2.
+Let kappa=n/4+2, t_i=kappa*i modn. At each slice x1=i take the nonempty
+NONWRAPPING x2 chart intervals from
+ [0,t_i-1], {t_i}, [t_i+1,n-1],
+omitting an empty interval, and x3 intervals {0},[1,n-1]. All cell x1
+factors are {i}. Use this exact partition in both original channels,
+with each spatial component observed by (V|S|)^(-1/2)sum_S z_r,alpha.
+
+kappa is2 modulo4, hence gcd(kappa,n)=2. Its orbit consists of all even
+positions, each visited twice over n slices. Thus t_i=n-1 never occurs;
+t_i=0 occurs exactly twice, and other t_i are interior. There are4 cells
+at each of those two slices and6 cells at each other slice, per channel.
+The full number of original rows is therefore
+ 2*3*[2*4+(n-2)*6]=36n-24.                                 (R)
+No wrapping support or merged/substituted observation is used in(R).
+
+CLAIM TO AUDIT
+Put L=log((n/4+1)/3). If
+ L >= 2^18 *6*148,                                         (T)
+there is a real nonzero actual-coexact z, all36n-24 means zero, with
+ Q(z)<(7/16)c||z||^2<c||z||^2.
+Consequently this particular nonwrapping O(n)-row moving refinement cannot
+restore target c with any finite quadratic penalty on its actual means.
+The condition is huge and unoptimized; powers of2 satisfying it exist.
+No failure of all O(n) partitions or canonical nlogn optimum is asserted.
+
+1. COVER THE ACTUAL TERMINAL CORNERS, INCLUDING NEW CHART BOUNDARIES
+For an interior t_i the actual terminal x2 endpoints are t_i-1,t_i,n-1;
+for t_i=0 they are0,n-1. The x3 terminal endpoints are0,n-1 in every slice.
+Define the SIX-ENTRY TAGGED list G_i by the three x2 formulas
+ t_i, t_i-1 modn, n-1,
+each paired with x3=0,n-1, keeping tags even if spatial positions coincide.
+Thus G_i covers every actual refined-cell corner, including the stationary
+chart boundary n-1. At t_i=0 some entries coincide; this does not change
+the six tags or introduce new observations. No constant actual cell count
+or bijection between the varying-size actual corner sets is assumed.
+
+Since4*kappa=n+8, match G_i to G_(i+4) by the same six tags. The four
+entries of types t_i,t_i-1 translate by8 modulo n and the two entries of
+type n-1 stay fixed. All matched periodic transverse l1 distances are<=8.
+This explicit matching exists across the longitudinal seam as well.
+
+2. EXPLICIT CUTOFF AND TAGGED WINDOW ESTIMATES
+Use the finite radial function from257A Section3, on Y=Zn^2:
+ R=n/4, rho_p=periodic l-infinity distance,
+ f_p=clip_[0,1](log((rho_p+1)/3)/L).
+Its directly proved original counting estimates are
+ E_Y(f_p)<=64/L, ||1-f_p||_Y^2<=4n^2/L^2.                  (1)
+These particular estimates, not a presumed abstract capacity/gap hypothesis,
